NOTES={1745: 'Title Implementation of AI to Robot Dynamics; printed Lecture Number 55 and footer 1.', 1746: 'Contents roadmap: dynamics revision, FFNN, forward dynamics pipeline, MLP inverse dynamics on 2R, and DeLaN inverse dynamics on 2R. Footer 2.', 1747: 'Introduction lists imperfect mass/inertia/friction, backlash, flexibility/compliance/contact, difficult soft/legged/deformable systems; networks approximate forward/inverse/friction/residuals and may adapt. Classical dynamics does not inherently require perfect known parameters, and learned adaptation is conditional, not automatic. Footer 3.', 1748: 'Full equation M(Θ)Θddot+C(Θ,Θdot)+G(Θ)=τ. C is the Coriolis/centrifugal generalized-force vector in this notation, not an unmultiplied n×n matrix. All position/velocity/acceleration/M/C/G/τ definitions inspected. Inverse map takes positions, velocities and accelerations to torque; feedforward/computed torque/tracking applications. No explicit friction/contact term in the displayed nominal equation. Footer 4.'}
NOTES.update({1749: 'Forward dynamics input (Θ,Θdot,τ), output acceleration, Θddot=M inverse(τ−C−G). Applications simulation, RL, MPC, digital twins. Motion requires integration after instantaneous acceleration; invertibility/model scope declared. Footer 5.', 1750: 'Three FFNN motivations: universal approximation, data-driven without exact inertial/friction equations, differentiability for optimization/autodiff/physics. Box names Deep Lagrangian, Hamiltonian and Physics-Informed networks. Approximation capacity is not a training/extrapolation guarantee; ReLU is piecewise differentiable and later higher derivatives need care. Footer 6.', 1751: 'Forward 2R diagram: six inputs θ1 θ2 θdot1 θdot2 τ1 τ2, two illustrative 32-neuron hidden layers, ReLU/tanh labels, two acceleration outputs. Arm diagram θ1 relative horizontal, θ2 relative first-link extension, lengths l1/l2 and masses m1 at elbow,m2 distal; torques τ1/τ2. Footer 7.', 1752: 'Phase1 diagram: neural identifier MLP6–30–20–2, sigmoid and standard backprop; nominal dynamics dataset deliberately spans beyond operational region, parameters differ from real inertia/friction. Broad nominal pretraining to reported1.5millioniterations and averageerror<5%. Reported benchmark not reproduced and no universal stopping guarantee; labels true accelerations are nominal-model labels, not measurements. Synthetic exploration beyond operation is not permission to drive physical robot beyond limits. Footer 8.'})
NOTES.update({1753: 'Phase2 full diagram: random sinusoidal torques bounded by actuator limits, frequencies below half joint natural frequencies (≤5Hz in example),58000response data sets every5ms in physical operational region. Fine-tune pretrained model100iterations to reported<5%averageerror plateau; validate novel torques, ODE-integrate predicted accelerations to velocities/positions, compare real behavior. 5ms=200Hz;58000samples span289.995s between first/last if contiguous;NΔt=290s nominal acquisition duration. Frequency safety guidance is source-specific, not a proven safety guarantee. Footer 9.', 1754: '2R inverse dynamics problem: l1=l2=1m,m1=m2=1kg point masses at each link tip,g9.81m/s², MLP regression. Pictured Θ1 from horizontal and Θ2 relative link1 extension. Data box groups joint triples[(θ1,θdot1,θddot1),(θ2,θdot2,θddot2)] to torques. Learned model need not expose physical parameters at inference, but following synthetic training labels explicitly depend on known analytical parameters. Footer 10.', 1755: 'Analytical model generates training labels. Exact printed M11=(m1+m2)l1²+m2l2²+2m1l1l2cosθ2, M12=M21=m2l2²+m2l1l2cosθ2, M22=m2l2². The M11 cross coefficient prints m1, unlike the distal-point-mass derivation requiring m2. Equal source masses hide this defect; preserve and qualify it, not silently correct source. Full arm geometry and equations viewed. Footer 11.', 1756: 'h=m2l1l2sinθ2; C1=−h θdot2²−2h θdot1θdot2, C2=h θdot1². Gravity g1=(m1+m2)g l1cosθ1+m2g l2cos(θ1+θ2),g2=m2g l2cos(θ1+θ2). Complete row expansions τ1=M11θddot1+M12θddot2+C1+g1 and τ2=M21θddot1+M22θddot2+C2+g2. Gravity cos matches horizontal-angle reference. C is already vector, no extra velocity multiplication. Footer 12.'})
NOTES.update({1757: 'Dataset explicitly orders X=[θ1,θ2,θdot1,θdot2,θddot1,θddot2], y=[τ1,τ2], differs from earlier interleaved display but is consistent with later code. Angles±π,velocities±2π,accelerations±10;N50000. Independent joint-coordinate uniform sampling is not uniform Cartesian workspace sampling; arbitrary acceleration tuples are labels, not a dynamically integrated trajectory. Footer13.', 1758: 'All imports and full vectorized inverse_dynamics function visually read. Code M11 cross term uses correct2*m2*L1*L2*cos(q2), contrasting printed m1 onp1755. M12 shared for both off-diagonals; h/C/g and torque rows matchp1756. Params L1=L2=m1=m2=1,g_acc9.81. Function used to generate synthetic labels, not directly invoked inside learned prediction. Footer14.', 1759: 'Six independent np.random.uniform calls, no np random seed in source; N50000. column_stack yields X50000×6,Y50000×2; train_test_splittest_size.1,random_state42 means45000train5000test. Split seed does not seed generated data. Uniform random draws do not guarantee evenly spaced values. Footer15.', 1760: 'Full Pipeline(StandardScaler,MLPRegressor) code: hidden256,256,128,tanh,max_iter500,learning_rate_init1e−3,random_state42,verboseTrue;fitX_trY_tr. Inputscaler fitted inside pipeline ontraining only, targetsnot scaled. max_iter is maximum epochs for default stochastic Adam, may stop early, not guaranteed500updates. StandardScaler unitvariance qualificationzero-variancefeatures. Footer16.'})
NOTES.update({1761: 'Prediction5000teststates, code computes per-joint sqrt(mean(square(error))). Reportedoutputs0.6311Nm and0.3734Nm. Adjacent Error metric drawing omits mean, giving per-sample absoluteerror rather than datasetRMSE; preservecode/diagram distinction. PlainMLP noarchitectureenforcedSPD massmatrix. Footer17.', 1762: 'Two full timeplots:blue solid true vsred dashed NNpredictedtorques, shoulderabove/elbowbelow,time0–about12.6s. Visiblesmallnonzeroresiduals aroundextrema/transitions; no exacttrajectorycode onslide. Link points to course GitHub notebook location; no originalnotebookretrieval attempted. Figuredoesnot establishuniformbound orclosedloopstability. Footer18.', 1763: 'DeLaNlearnsconfiguration-only subnetoutputsH(q) symmetricpositive-definite andV(q),thenEuler–Lagrangeproducesτ. Lastclaimonlyqinput applies to subnetworks,notcompleteinverse-dynamicsτwhichstillneedsdq/ddq. Footer19.', 1764: 'Exact equationτ=Hddq+[Hdot dq−1/2(∂T/∂q)^T]+∂V/∂q;bottomlabelsT=dq^T H dq askineticenergywithout1/2. With that doubled-energydefinition the torqueexpression is consistent,butlabelkineticenergywrong. ActualkineticK=.5dq^T H dqrequires−∂K/∂q. Nonconservativefriction/contactrequireadditionalforces;H,Vonlyisnominalconservativemodel. Footer20.', 1765: 'CompleteblueHpath/greenVpathflowchartandautogradarrowsviewed. HerekineticT=.5dq^T H dqbutCblockstillHdotdq−.5∂T/∂q, anactualfactor-of-twodefectcomparedwithEuler–Lagrange. Inputsgraphicshowsqonlybutderivative/accelerationbranchesneedvelocities/accelerations. Vgradientfeedsgravity;threecomponents sumtorque. Footer21.', 1766: 'DeLaNsame2Rparameters;PyTorchvs sklearn,physicsstructurevsblackbox,qonlytosubnets. N5000vsMLP50000illustratesreporteddataefficiencybutisnotuniversal10×guaranteeorfaircomparisonwithoutcontrolledconditions. Footer22.', 1767: 'FullPyTorch/nn,NumPy,Matplotlib,Adamimports;allanalyticalinverse_dynamicscodeagainusescorrectm2crosscoefficient. AdamAdaptiveMomentEstimationusesparameterwisemomentupdates;torque-labelgeneratorseparatefromlearnedsubnetworks. Footer23.', 1768: 'N5000sixuniformdraws,tauvectorizedlabels;Q,DQ,DDQ,TAUeach5000×2float32tensors. Sequentialslice n_tr=int(.9*N) gives4500train500test, preservingalignedindices;nottrain_test_splitrandom_state42. Drawsareindependentrandom,notorderedtrajectory. NoNumPy/PyTorchseedsvisible. Footer24.'})
NOTES.update({1769: 'Full training excerpt inspected: DeLaN2R(hidden_size=64,n_layers=2), Adam lr=0.001 and weight_decay=0.0001, MSELoss, 500 epochs, batch size128, n_batches=max(1,4500//128)=35. A new permutation is made each epoch; 4480 examples are used and20 are omitted per epoch, not necessarily the same20. zero_grad precedes backward and optimizer.step. The DeLaN2R class definition is absent from the entire lecture, so the excerpt is not standalone executable. Footer25.', 1770: 'Training-loss plot has logarithmic MSE vertical axis and epochs0–500. Large initial decrease, slower later decline and nonmonotonic spikes are visible. Training loss alone is not held-out accuracy or a guaranteed generalization bound. Footer26.', 1771: 'Prediction calls model.eval, enables autograd inside the forward calculation, then detaches the returned torque. eval is not a replacement for gradient mode and does not perform evaluation by itself. Per-joint test RMSE code is correct. Reported0.2826Nm and0.1895Nm are lower than the earlier reported MLP values, with5000versus50000generated samples; no controlled-run universal advantage is proven. Footer27.', 1772: 'All sinusoidal test code inspected:300endpoint-inclusive samples0 to4π; q1=sin(t),q2=.5sin(2t),dq1=cos(t),dq2=cos(2t),ddq1=−sin(t),ddq2=−2sin(2t). Analytical labels use the same inverse dynamics; Q_tr_/DQ_tr_/DDQ_tr_ are new300×2 float32 trajectory tensors, not training tensors despite names. predict(...).numpy assumes the detached result is on CPU. Footer28.', 1773: 'Two full sinusoidal torque plots inspected: blue true and red dashed DeLaN shoulder above/elbow below, close but not identically equal. Exact reproduction needs the omitted class and trained weights. Course notebook link is visible but no retrieval attempted. Footer29.', 1774: 'Summary introduces RNEA and ABA names, parameter/rigid-body assumptions, learned models and physics structure. Forward shorthand τ→acceleration omits conditioning on current q,dq. Energy conservation requires unforced conservative assumptions; for applied torque the proper statement is power balance, and dissipation needs additional terms. Improved generalization and future foundation/self-updating models are prospects, not unconditional guarantees. Footer30.', 1775: 'Three references only: Craig2005, Lutter/Ritter/Peters DeLaN ICLR2019, and Fang/Dissanayake forward-dynamics ICRA1998. Footer31.', 1776: 'Thank-you closing page, footer32.', 1753: 'Phase2 diagram: random sinusoidal torques are bounded by actuator limits; frequencies are below half the joint natural frequencies (≤5 Hz in this example). It reports58000 responses at5 ms intervals inside the physical operating region. Fine-tuning uses the pretrained model for a reported100 iterations to an average error below5% and a plateau. Validation uses novel torques, ODE integration and comparison with real motion. The5 ms interval is200 Hz;58000 contiguous samples span289.995 s from first to last, whereas NΔt is290 s. These are source-specific conditions, not a general physical safety guarantee. Footer9.', 1754: 'The2R inverse-dynamics example has l1=l2=1 m, m1=m2=1 kg as point masses at the link tips, and g=9.81 m/s². MLP regression takes joint positions, velocities and accelerations to two torques. The figure measures θ1 from horizontal and θ2 from the first-link extension. Its input box interleaves joint triples, unlike the later grouped code order. The learned predictor need not expose parameters at inference, but synthetic label generation uses known parameters. Footer10.', 1755: 'The printed mass matrix has M11=(m1+m2)l1²+m2l2²+2m1l1l2cosθ2, M12=M21=m2l2²+m2l1l2cosθ2, and M22=m2l2². The cross term in M11 prints m1, but the illustrated distal point-mass model requires m2. Equal example masses mask the discrepancy. The full geometry and all equations were read. Footer11.', 1756: 'The slide defines h=m2l1l2sinθ2, C1=−h θdot2²−2h θdot1θdot2 and C2=h θdot1². Gravity entries are g1=(m1+m2)g l1cosθ1+m2g l2cos(θ1+θ2) and g2=m2g l2cos(θ1+θ2). Both torque row expansions include inertia, velocity-product and gravity terms. Cosine gravity matches the horizontal angle reference. C is already a force vector, so it is not multiplied by velocity again. Footer12.', 1757: 'Dataset order is X=[θ1,θ2,θdot1,θdot2,θddot1,θddot2], y=[τ1,τ2]. It differs from the earlier interleaved display but matches later code. Angles span±π, velocities±2π and accelerations±10; N=50000. Uniform joint-coordinate sampling is not uniform Cartesian workspace sampling. Independent random state tuples are not a dynamically integrated trajectory. Footer13.', 1758: 'All imports and the complete vectorized inverse_dynamics function were read. Code M11 uses2*m2*L1*L2*cos(q2), contrasting the m1 in the equation slide. The symmetric off-diagonal, h, C, gravity and torque rows match the physical point-mass model. Parameters are all unit masses/lengths with g_acc=9.81. The function generates synthetic labels, not the learned model’s prediction. Footer14.', 1759: 'Six independent np.random.uniform calls have no displayed NumPy seed. column_stack gives X shape50000×6 and Y shape50000×2. train_test_split with test_size=0.1 and random_state=42 produces45000 training and5000 test rows. The split seed does not seed earlier data generation. Random uniform draws are not guaranteed equally spaced. Footer15.', 1760: 'Pipeline combines StandardScaler and MLPRegressor with hidden widths256,256,128, tanh, max_iter500, learning_rate_init0.001, random_state42 and verboseTrue. The scaler is fitted to training inputs inside the pipeline, not targets or held-out rows. max_iter is a maximum epoch count for the default stochastic optimizer, not a guarantee of exactly500 updates. Zero-variance features qualify the unit-variance summary. Footer16.', 1761: 'Code computes per-joint sqrt(mean(square(error))) over5000 test states. Reported RMSE values are0.6311 and0.3734 N·m. The adjacent graphic omits the mean, showing a per-sample absolute error instead. A plain MLP does not structurally guarantee a positive-definite mass matrix. Footer17.', 1762: 'Both time plots were read: blue solid true torque and red dashed prediction, shoulder above and elbow below, time0 to about12.6 s. Small nonzero deviations are visible. Exact trajectory generation is not supplied on this page. The course notebook URL is visible but was not retrieved. These plots do not establish a uniform error bound or closed-loop stability. Footer18.', 1763: 'Configuration-only subnetworks output a symmetric positive-definite H(q) and potential V(q), then Euler–Lagrange relations produce torque. The last only-q-input claim is valid for subnetworks, not the complete inverse-dynamics calculation, which still needs velocity and acceleration. Footer19.', 1764: 'Torque is printed as Hddq+Hdotdq−0.5∇T+∇V, while the bottom defines T=dqᵀHdq and calls it kinetic energy. The torque expression is consistent with this doubled-energy definition, but physical kinetic energy is K=0.5dqᵀHdq and then the subtraction is −∇K. H and V alone describe the stated conservative model, not arbitrary friction or contact forces. Footer20.', 1765: 'The complete blue H path, green V path, autodiff arrows and summation were inspected. This page defines kinetic T=0.5dqᵀHdq but still subtracts0.5∇T in the velocity-product component, creating a factor-of-two defect. The position-only input graphic omits velocity and acceleration supplied to the physical computation. V contributes its gradient to gravity. Footer21.', 1766: 'The same2R model is used for a physics-structured PyTorch implementation rather than the scikit-learn black-box MLP. Only subnetworks use q alone. The5000-versus50000 dataset example is presented as data efficiency, but is not a universal tenfold guarantee or controlled comparison by itself. Footer22.', 1767: 'PyTorch, nn, NumPy, Matplotlib and Adam imports and the complete analytical label generator were inspected. The M11 cross coefficient is m2. Adam is expanded as Adaptive Moment Estimation. The label generator is distinct from the learned subnetworks. Footer23.', 1768: 'The5000 generated samples become Q,DQ,DDQ,TAU tensors of shape5000×2 and dtype float32. Aligned sequential slices at n_tr=int(0.9*N) produce4500 training and500 test samples. This is not the earlier train_test_split operation. No NumPy or PyTorch seed is displayed. Footer24.'})
NOTES.update({1747: 'The introduction lists nonlinear friction, backlash, cable flexibility, compliance and contact among difficult effects. Learning targets include forward/inverse dynamics and residuals. Adaptation requires data and an update mechanism; it is not automatic. Printed footer 3 inspected separately.', 1750: 'All approximation, data-driven and differentiability bullets were inspected, together with the box naming Deep Lagrangian, Hamiltonian and physics-informed networks. Representation capacity and derivative availability do not establish trained accuracy. Printed footer 6 inspected separately.', 1752: 'Phase 1 specifies an MLP with widths 6–30–20–2, sigmoid activation and backpropagation. Nominal synthetic data span beyond the physical operating region. The reported 1.5 million iterations and average error below 5% are experiment-specific, not a universal stop guarantee or permission to exceed real actuator limits. Printed footer 8 inspected separately.', 1753: 'Phase 2 uses bounded sinusoidal torques, frequencies below half the joint natural frequency and an example cap of 5 Hz. It reports 58,000 samples at 5 ms intervals, then 100 fine-tuning iterations. Validation uses novel torque inputs, ODE integration and real-motion comparison. The sample rate is 200 Hz; endpoint span is 289.995 s under consecutive sampling. Printed footer 9 inspected separately.', 1757: 'The ordered input is [q1,q2,q̇1,q̇2,q̈1,q̈2], with two torque targets. Angles span ±π, velocities ±2π and accelerations ±10. There are 50,000 independent random state tuples. Uniform joint coordinates do not imply uniform Cartesian endpoint density or a connected motion trajectory. Printed footer 13 inspected separately.', 1758: 'Every import and the complete vectorized inverse_dynamics function were inspected. Its M11 cross coefficient uses m2, unlike the m1 printed on page 1755. All C, gravity and row-expansion terms were checked. Unit masses and lengths and g=9.81 are explicit. Printed footer 14 inspected separately.', 1759: 'Six independent NumPy uniform draws have no displayed dataset seed. Column stacking gives X with 50,000 rows and six columns and Y with two columns. The 90:10 split has random_state=42, which does not retroactively seed data generation. Printed footer 15 inspected separately.', 1760: 'Pipeline contains StandardScaler and MLPRegressor with hidden widths 256,256,128, tanh, max_iter=500, learning_rate_init=0.001 and random_state=42. Training-only input statistics are used; targets are not scaled. max_iter is a maximum epoch count, not a guaranteed number of updates. Printed footer 16 inspected separately.', 1761: 'The code computes per-joint RMSE by averaging squared errors before taking the square root. Reported values are 0.6311 and 0.3734 N·m. The adjacent metric graphic lacks the mean operation. No positive-definite inertia structure is imposed on the plain torque MLP. Printed footer 17 inspected separately.', 1762: 'Both complete torque plots were inspected: true blue and predicted red dashed traces, shoulder above and elbow below, time from 0 to about 12.6 s. Small nonzero deviations are visible. The course notebook link was not retrieved; no closed-loop stability inference is supported by this plot alone. Printed footer 18 inspected separately.', 1763: 'H(q) is described as a symmetric positive-definite inertia matrix and V(q) as scalar potential. Configuration-only input applies to these subnetworks; the full Euler–Lagrange torque still needs velocity and acceleration. Printed footer 19 inspected separately.', 1764: 'The printed equation subtracts half the gradient of T, while T is defined as q̇ᵀHq̇ without one-half and labelled kinetic energy. This is consistent only if T is twice physical kinetic energy. Physical K=0.5q̇ᵀHq̇ requires subtraction of its full gradient. Printed footer 20 inspected separately.', 1765: 'All blue H and green V branches, derivative arrows and torque summation were inspected. Here T already includes one-half, but its gradient is halved again: a genuine normalization discrepancy. The position-only input drawing also omits the motion variables needed by the physical computation. Printed footer 21 inspected separately.', 1766: 'The same point-mass 2R model is learned with structured PyTorch rather than the black-box scikit-learn MLP. The reported 5,000 versus 50,000 samples illustrate possible data efficiency, not a universal tenfold guarantee. Printed footer 22 inspected separately.', 1767: 'Imports and the complete analytical torque generator were read. The M11 cross coefficient is m2. Adam is expanded as Adaptive Moment Estimation. The analytical label generator is separate from the learned H and V subnetworks. Printed footer 23 inspected separately.', 1768: 'The 5,000 samples produce Q,DQ,DDQ,TAU tensors, each with two float32 columns. Aligned slices give 4,500 training rows and 500 test rows. No NumPy or PyTorch seed is displayed. Printed footer 24 inspected separately.', 1769: 'The class call uses width 64 and two hidden layers; Adam has learning rate 0.001 and weight decay 0.0001. MSELoss, 500 epochs, batch size 128 and floor-divided 35 batches are printed. Each epoch uses 4,480 rows and drops 20 shuffled rows. zero_grad, backward and step ordering was checked. DeLaN2R itself is absent from the lecture. Printed footer 25 inspected separately.', 1770: 'The full logarithmic training-loss plot was read. It falls sharply at first and more slowly later, with visible upward fluctuations. This is training MSE, not test RMSE or a proof of generalization. Printed footer 26 inspected separately.', 1771: 'Prediction sets evaluation mode, enables autograd for energy derivatives, and detaches the returned torque. eval does not disable autograd. Reported per-joint RMSE values are 0.2826 and 0.1895 N·m, distinct from any independently reproduced output. Printed footer 27 inspected separately.', 1772: 'Every trajectory line was read: 300 endpoint-inclusive times from 0 to 4π; q1=sin t, q2=0.5sin 2t, velocities cos t and cos 2t, accelerations −sin t and −2sin 2t. New trajectory tensors have 300 rows and two columns despite their training-like names. NumPy conversion assumes CPU output. Printed footer 28 inspected separately.', 1773: 'Both complete DeLaN torque comparison plots were inspected. True blue and predicted red dashed curves nearly overlap but are not identical. Exact execution requires the absent class and trained state; the course notebook link was not retrieved. Printed footer 29 inspected separately.', 1774: 'The summary names RNEA and ABA, contrasts nominal and learned dynamics, and discusses physics structure and future models. Forward dynamics still conditions on current position and velocity. Energy conservation needs a zero-power conservative qualification; powered motion follows a work–energy balance. Printed footer 30 inspected separately.', 1775: 'Three bibliographic references only: Craig, the 2019 DeLaN paper, and the 1998 forward-dynamics neural-model paper. Printed footer 31 inspected separately.', 1776: 'Thank-you closing page. Printed footer 32 inspected separately.'})
